WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.850
Mark Fischbach, better known as Markiplier,
is one of the biggest YouTube stars in the

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.189
world, with over 16 million subscribers.

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:12.790
But while all his fans are familiar with his
high energy reactions in his Let's Play videos,

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.450
there's actually a lot more to him than just
shouting and playing games.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.439
Here are eight things the world needs to know
about Markiplier.

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:21.439
Regular guy

00:00:21.439 --> 00:00:25.779
Before he became one of the internet's most
famous personalities, Markiplier was just

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:26.849
a regular dude.

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:32.169
Born in Honolulu, Hawaii, he studied engineering
at the University of Cincinnati.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:36.860
But he didn't end up graduating, instead using
his engineering skills to dominate building

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.170
games like Poly Bridge while entertaining
his fans.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.510
Sounds like a win-win.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.589
He taught Jimmy Kimmel the ropes

00:00:43.589 --> 00:00:48.210
Late night show personality Jimmy Kimmel once
said that he thought that watching Let's Play

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.179
videos was a waste of time.

00:00:50.179 --> 00:00:54.640
After the internet ganged up on him, Kimmel
invited Markiplier and fellow Let's Play star

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.649
MissesMae to teach him the ropes and explain
just what he was missing.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:01.460
"Hey, will you tell the people, not to kill
me?"

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:01.960
"No."

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:02.580
"No.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.100
No."

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.580
We're still waiting for Kimmel's own Let's
Play channel to launch, but this seems like

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.060
a pretty good start anyway.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.009
He's afraid of mannequins

00:01:10.009 --> 00:01:13.610
Like most people, there are things out in
the world that scare Mark.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.850
More specifically, mannequins and dolls give
him a major case of the heebie-jeebies.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:17.850
"Hun.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.600
Why are they all staring at me?

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.600
That is unsettling.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.600
Get away.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.600
Oh no.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.689
Why are they all staring at me?

00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:26.689
Creepy creepy creepy."

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:31.630
That may not sound like a big deal, but as
anyone who watches his channel knows, mannequins

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.020
and dolls seem to appear a lot more often
in video games than you might expect.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:40.479
Which is great for our entertainment, but
not so great for Markiplier's anxiety levels.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.480
"AHHHH!

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.700
GET OUT OF HERE GET OUT OF HERE!

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:47.520
OH NO!

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.960
GET OUT OF HERE!

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.090
OH NO"

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.270
Margarita Man

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:56.049
Mark was presented with a Taco Trophy — an
object that we envy deeply — by Rachael

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.929
Ray, for having created an amazing margarita.

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:03.799
Turns out that Markiplier once worked as a
bartender, which explains why he's so familiar

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:07.520
with how to make a great one, knowledge he
shared with his thirsty fans.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.510
"And you don't need to add a lot of zest to
it.

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:15.770
You just need to make one, and garnish it,
because presentation is 50% of everything."

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:17.510
He took a hiatus

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:22.300
Mark took a brief hiatus from YouTube following
the death of a close friend of his, Daniel

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.300
Kyre.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:28.280
Daniel was part of Cyndago, a comedy group
on YouTube that focused on dark humor, usually

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.830
of satirical nature.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:34.070
Daniel reached out to Mark to collaborate
with him on projects, and they ended up becoming

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.910
roommates and close friends.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:41.490
On September 18, 2015, Kyre passed away from
brain damage after an attempted suicide.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:45.560
"Daniel, was such an influence on what we
did.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.870
He was such an inspiration for what I did.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:52.560
Mark went dark on YouTube for a about a month
before returning to his work.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.340
Misery loves company

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.920
This might cause you to look away in abject
horror, but Mark has joint hypermobility in

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.241
his legs, meaning that he can move his knees
beyond their normal range, as though he just

00:03:03.241 --> 00:03:05.450
got hit with a sledgehammer by Kathy Bates.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:10.370
As far as party tricks go, this one is downright
repulsive, but you also kind of can't look

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.220
away once he starts doing it.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.220
"Zoinks!"

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.980
The Snapchat incident

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.090
In 2015, a fan claimed that Mark had abused
his power of celebrity and exploited her for

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:25.680
nude photos on the popular app Snapchat, screenshotting
a topless photo that she accidentally sent

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.680
to him.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.650
Mark later denied the allegations, claiming
that the fan had continually sent him nude

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:35.160
photos despite his requests that she stop,
and that he never took a screenshot of any

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.160
of them.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.450
The incident resulted in Markiplier quitting
Snapchat for good.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.880
It's just a banana

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:47.030
For April Fool's Day 2016, Mark uploaded a
video titled "Mark Contemplates a Banana for

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.030
5 Minutes."

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:52.130
The joke apparently was that he is so popular,
he could literally post anything at all and

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.470
people would still watch.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:57.260
Well, the joke's on us, because he's been
proven right, as more than two and a half

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.830
million people have watched him watch that
banana.

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.900
No spoilers, it still hasn't done anything
particularly appealing.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.370
Thanks for watching!

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.180
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.350
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

